                <pb facs="0390" n="292" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg292"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum handed to Acting Secretary Hill by the
                        Chinese Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chinese Legation</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-09-13"><hi rendition="#italic">September 13,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">Cablegram from Earl Li Hung Chang,
                        dated Shanghai, September 12, 1900, to Minister Wu, who received it on the
                        evening of the same day.</hi></p>
                <p>Your telegram of September 11 received. I have proper credentials, with full and
                    authoritative powers for opening and conducting negotiations with the several
                    powers. The life and property of Americans in China will be respected.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
